  "question": {
    "text": "A gas is kept in a container having walls which are thermally non-conducting. Initially the gas has a volume of $800 \\mathrm{~cm}^3$ and temperature $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The change in temperature when the gas is adiabatically compressed to $200 \\mathrm{~cm}^3$ is :<br/>(Take $\\gamma=1.5: \\gamma$ is the ratio of specific heats at constant pressure and at constant volume)"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "327 K",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "600 K",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "522 K",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "300 K",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{V}_1=800 \\mathrm{~cm}^3 \\quad \\mathrm{~V}_2=200 \\mathrm{~cm}^3 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~T}_1=300 \\mathrm{~K}<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>for adiabatic<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{TV}^{\\gamma-1}=\\text { const. } \\\\\n& (300)(800)^{1.5-1}=\\mathrm{T}_2(200)^{1.5-1} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~T}_2=300\\left[\\frac{800}{200}\\right]^{0.5}=300 \\times\\left(2^2\\right)^{1 / 2} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~T}_2=600 \\mathrm{~K} \\\\\n& \\Delta \\mathrm{~T}=600-300=300 \\mathrm{~K}<br/>\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}